[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n5_osric"
text = "# DRAFT
# Osric at dusk, at the kitchen fire (night 5, clear and cold). The fast is over: bread tonight, and the heel kept back.
# Smiling. If the porter saw his face under the mask last night (osric_mask), he knows this face; Osric acts as if nothing happened.
# Where he was last night: the wrong question (Suspicion +5). Saying he saw his face: Suspicion +15, and Osric ends the talk.
== start
(Osric is at the kitchen fire, flour to the elbow, the smell of new bread all round him. He beams at you.)
Osric {glad}: The porter! The fast's done, God be thanked. Bread tonight, and I've kept the heel back for you.
-> mask [if osric_mask]
-> topics

== mask
(It's the face you saw in the fog last night, with the horns pushed back off it. It's smiling at you.)
-> topics

== again
Osric {glad}: Back again? You can smell it. Patience, porter. Not till the bell.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n5_osric_fast] Why was the fast lifted, brother? -> fast
* [if not n5_osric_where] Where were you last night, brother? -> where
* [if osric_mask] [if not n5_osric_face] I saw your face in the fog last night, brother. -> face

== fast [set n5_osric_fast]
Osric {glad}: Father Abbot lifted it after Prime. A night and a day of nothing, and half the house couldn't stand at Lauds.
Osric {glad, smile}: Eat tonight, porter. All of it. You'll want your strength.
-> topics

# The wrong question to the wrong brother (design doc): Suspicion +5.
== where [set n5_osric_where] [suspicion 5]
Osric {glad, smile}: Abed, in the dormitory, listening to my belly. Like every Christian in the house. Where else would I be?
(He goes on kneading.)
Osric {amused}: Ask the brother in the next bed. He'll tell you how I snore.
-> topics

# Accusing a cultist to his face: Suspicion +15.
== face [set n5_osric_face] [suspicion 15]
(He laughs, a big warm laugh. The dough under his hands doesn't stop.)
Osric {amused, smile}: My face? In the fog? Porter, you've been fasting. A hungry man sees faces in his porridge.
Osric {glad}: Eat your bread tonight. All of it. You'll see clearer for it.
-> end

== leave
Osric {glad}: The heel's yours, porter! Don't be late!
"
